implementationPlan.description:
Panel side, in moe-vscode/src/panels/TaskDetailPanel.ts. Add no value import; touch client.releaseTask only inside the handler, because three peer tests load the panel with strict require maps and strict client stubs (mem:gotcha-vscode-panel-strict-require-map).
- Module constants copied exactly from moe-jetbrains/src/main/resources/messages/MoeBundle.properties:
  - RELEASE_AGENT_LABEL = 'Release Agent' (moe.button.releaseAgent);
  - RELEASED_FROM_BOARD = 'Released from board' (moe.message.releasedInUI);
  - RELEASE_AGENT_CONFIRM = the moe.message.releaseAgent template, kept with its {0}/{1} placeholders and its em dash.
- Format it in ONE pass, `RELEASE_AGENT_CONFIRM.replace(/\{([01])\}/g, (_, i) => i === '0' ? workerId : title)`, so a worker id containing "{1}" or "$&" is never re-substituted. The modal is plain text, so never escapeHtml it.
- In getWebviewContent's actions bar, render `<button class="btn btn-secondary" id="releaseAgentBtn">Release Agent</button>` right after the reopen button. Render it only when nonBlankString(task.assignedWorkerId) !== null; that is JetBrains' isNullOrBlank rule, for any status.
- New `case 'releaseAgent':` in handleWebviewMessage, inside the existing try/catch:
  - read the FRESH task with this.findTask(); the actions bar is static, so the button can outlive the assignment;
  - if there is no task or its assignedWorkerId is blank, `vscode.window.showInformationMessage('No agent is assigned to this task.')` and stop;
  - otherwise `const choice = await vscode.window.showWarningMessage(formatted text with the raw assignedWorkerId and task.title, { modal: true }, RELEASE_AGENT_LABEL)`;
  - only when choice === RELEASE_AGENT_LABEL call `this.client.releaseTask(this.taskId, RELEASED_FROM_BOARD)`;
  - when that returns false, `vscode.window.showWarningMessage('Not connected to Moe daemon — agent was not released.')`;
  - show no success toast (JetBrains shows none; the board update is the feedback).
- Error handling: an exception still lands in the handler's existing catch (showErrorMessage).

Page side, in moe-vscode/media/taskDetail.js, next to the Reopen block:
```
var releaseAgentBtn = document.getElementById('releaseAgentBtn');
if (releaseAgentBtn) {
    releaseAgentBtn.addEventListener('click', function() {
        vscodeApi.postMessage({ type: 'releaseAgent' });
    });
}
```
- The guard is required, because the button exists only for an assigned task. Its error handling is that guard: an unassigned page must load without throwing.
- Send nothing else; the panel reads the worker id and title from fresh state.
- Leave the live-update handler alone: the actions bar stays static, like approve, reject and reopen.

Adversarial self-review of this task's diff, the only review step.
- Would a test fail if:
  - the button rendered for a whitespace-only id;
  - the handler released on dismiss;
  - it used the stale render-time worker id;
  - the modal text were HTML-escaped (the title has quotes, < and &);
  - placeholders were replaced in two passes;
  - the not-connected branch were dropped;
  - the page posted on load, or the button had no guard?
- Any value import added, or a client member touched outside the handler?
- Confirm with `git status --porcelain` that the task touched only moe-vscode/src/panels/TaskDetailPanel.ts, moe-vscode/media/taskDetail.js and moe-vscode/tests/task-release.test.cjs. Peers own every other dirty path: never revert, stage or commit them.
- Report the three files in complete_step.modifiedFiles.
